course: dictionary
lesson: 1511
title: The cello
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A cello is a large string instrument. You play it sitting down, with the cello held between your knees, and you draw a bow across its strings. «The violin, viola, cello and double bass are all string instruments played with a bow or plucked.» Cello is a noun: one cello, two cellos.
explain: Read the words around it to learn more. «Bigger ones play lower notes, and the cello and double bass are so big that they stand on the floor instead of resting under the chin like a violin.» So the cello is bigger than a violin, and it plays lower, warmer notes.
explain: The string family goes from high to low: «In the string family bigger instruments play lower: from highest to lowest they are violin, viola, cello and double bass.» A person who plays the cello is called a cellist.
fact: A cello is a large musical instrument with four strings.
fact: You play a cello sitting down, with it held between your knees.
fact: Cello is a noun: one cello, two cellos.
fact: A person who plays the cello is called a cellist.
fact: In an orchestra, the cellos sit near the front.
exercise: What is a cello? | A small drum you hit with sticks | A bow for hanging on a wall | A type of cold wind | *A large musical instrument with four strings
exercise: «In the string family bigger instruments play lower: from highest to lowest they are violin, viola, cello and double bass.» Which instrument plays the lowest notes? | *Double bass | Viola | Violin | Cello
exercise: How do you play a cello? | Standing up, with it resting under your chin | *Sitting down, with it held between your knees | Hitting it with sticks | Blowing into a mouthpiece
test: What do you call a person who plays the cello? | Drummer | Trumpeter | *Cellist | Flautist
test: «Bigger ones play lower notes.» So compared with a violin, a cello plays | *Lower notes | No notes at all | Only quiet notes | Higher notes
exam: In the family photo of strings, from small to huge, which one is the biggest? | Viola | *Double bass | Cello | Violin
